<div class="guide-styles" data-ay-injected="true" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 5 Best in Slot Gear list for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, BoE World drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Phase 5</h2>Enhancement <a class="icontiny c7" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/shaman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_shaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shaman</span></a> Tier 10 set has great bonuses in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70830/item-shaman-t10-enhancement-2p-bonus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_misc_emotionhappy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Shaman T10 Enhancement 2P Bonus</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70832/item-shaman-t10-enhancement-4p-bonus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_misc_emotionhappy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Shaman T10 Enhancement 4P Bonus</span></a> combined with excellent stats and item level, which you will want to get as quickly as possible. The 4-piece bonus in particular incentivizes reaching 5 <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=51532/maelstrom-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_maelstromweapon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maelstrom Weapon</span></a> as often as possible, thus <b>discouraging casting spells at partial stacks and diminishing the relevance of weaving</b>. <br/>
<br/>The extremely high levels of Critical Strike achieved in item level 264+ gear also <b>lessen the importance of weapon speed synching</b>, as you will be able to keep <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16284/flurry">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_ghoulfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry</span></a> up constantly, regardless. <br/>
<br/>Having a <b>
<span class="c4">Spell Power weapon to use as a mid-fight swap</span> to snapshot Spell Power</b> into your <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=2894/fire-elemental-totem">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_elemental_totem.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fire Elemental Totem</span></a> and when focusing on area of effect damage with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=61657/fire-nova">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_sealoffire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fire Nova</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49271/chain-lightning">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_chainlightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chain Lightning</span></a> is still <b>
<span class="c4">highly recommended</span></b> as these spells scale with Spell Power instead of traditional melee stats (AP does convert to SP with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30814/mental-quickness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_mentalquickness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mental Quickness</span></a>, but only at a 30% rate).<br/>
<br/>You will want a Physical main-hand for single target scenarios <b>and</b> a Spell Power main-hand to snapshot your Fire Elemental and AoE scenarios. We present below gear setup suggestions and optimizations for focusing on single target or AoE but the <b>main benefit can be obtained at any time by simply <span class="c4">swapping your weapon mid-combat</span></b>.<br/>
<br/>In Wrath, 26.23 Hit Rating converts into 1% Spell Hit at level 70. Unfortunately, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30819/dual-wield-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwieldspecialization.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dual Wield Specialization</span></a> does <b>not</b> give Spell Hit, thus the cap is 17% Spell Hit from gear alone, which can be reduced to 14% (or 13% if you are Alliance due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a>) with the help of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33602/improved-faerie-fire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Improved Faerie Fire</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33193/misery">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_misery.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Misery</span></a>. Thus, the exact amount of Spell Hit you want from your gear depends on the content you are optimizing for, and your faction. As a Horde player in a raid, you will need 26.23 * 14 = 	367.22 rating in order to cap Spell Hit, for example.<br/>
<br/>You will also be well over the 8% special attack melee Hit cap by then, as although 32.78 Hit Rating is required for 1%, you get 6% for free with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30819/dual-wield-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwieldspecialization.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dual Wield Specialization</span></a>, thus only needing 32.78 * 2 = 65.56 rating. Extra Hit rating over specials cap will still increase your white hit damage and enable more <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=51532/maelstrom-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_maelstromweapon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maelstrom Weapon</span></a> procs, which is a strong benefit.<br/>
<br/>While gearing up, remember that you can also use <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/items/armor/min-level:232/side:2/class:7/weights:32:117:114:103:96:119:77:123:250:249:248:247:23:21:20/weight-values:4.65:2.64:1.07:1.3:1:1.65:1:1.31:53.333:53.333:53.333:100:1.64:1.53:1.1/group-by:slot?filter=24:238:86:61;3:4:11:3;0:4:0:0#chest">crafted gear</a> to fill in for any weaker gear slots!<br/>
<br/>
