<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons, Shields, Off-hands and Totems for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Phase 5</h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="1-handed-weapons-for-enhancement-shaman-dps-in-phase-5">1-Handed Weapons for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Phase 5</h4>Due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16284/flurry">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_ghoulfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry</span></a> having a 0.5 seconds cooldown on being consumed, <b>having weapons of matching speed</b> can be useful to minimize attack desynching and maximize your Flurry uptime. Some of the main-hand (MH) and off-hand (OH) weapons we list below have similar speeds and weapons with the same speed are meant to be used <b>together</b>, whenever possible. <b>
<span class="c4">Once you approach full Tier 10 gear, the extremely high amount of Critical Strike rating will cause Flurry to happen very frequently regardless, lowering the benefit of weapon speed synching.</span></b>
<br/>
<br/>Also, as much of an Enhancement <a class="icontiny c7" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/shaman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_shaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shaman</span></a>'s damage comes from spells that scale with Spell Power rather than Weapon DPS /<wbr/> Attack Power (other than <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30814/mental-quickness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_mentalquickness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mental Quickness</span></a>), picking up a caster weapon is recommended for trash or bosses with multiple adds, and it performs decently in single target as well.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="weapons-for-enhancement-shaman-dps-in-phase-5">Weapons for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Phase 5</h4>With the release of <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>, <b>Spell Power</b> weapons return to being used for AoE and cleave purposes, while <b>Physical</b> weapons can be put to good use in the many single-target encounters in the raid.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50734/royal-scepter-of-terenas-ii">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_115.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Royal Scepter of Terenas II</span></a> (which is also overall <b>single-target BiS</b>) and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50737/havocs-call-blade-of-lordaeron-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Havoc's Call, Blade of Lordaeron Kings</span></a> are the overall best setup, but two <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50737/havocs-call-blade-of-lordaeron-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Havoc's Call, Blade of Lordaeron Kings</span></a> are also very strong, although any of these options requires defeating the hardest boss in the game, and are thus expected to be a rare sight. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51939/telthas-dagger-of-the-blood-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_101.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tel'thas, Dagger of the Blood King</span></a> (AoE setup) or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50692/black-bruise">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_hand_33.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Black Bruise</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51941/pugius-fist-of-defiance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_hand_34.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pugius, Fist of Defiance</span></a> (ST setup) combined with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50710/keleseths-seducer">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_hand_33.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Keleseth's Seducer</span></a> are likely to be a more achievable option for most <a class="icontiny c7" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/shaman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_shaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shaman</span></a>s in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46035/aesuga-hand-of-the-ardent-champion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Aesuga, Hand of the Ardent Champion</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46097/caress-of-insanity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_91.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Caress of Insanity</span></a> are excellent starting weapons which can be farmed through dungeons.<br/>
